Write this week's Community Voices Document for the Ruby on Rails community forum (discuss.rubyonrails.org).

Week: <%= week.label %> (<%= week.starts_on.iso8601 %> to <%= week.ends_on.iso8601 %>)

## Instructions

Write the document in Markdown with exactly these four sections, in this order:

## Summary
Two or three sentences on what the community talked about this week.

## Top discussions this past week
A bulleted list of the most important discussions. Name each discussion's topic and say why it matters.

## Recurring themes
A bulleted list of themes that came up in more than one discussion.

## Predictions for next week
A bulleted list of three predictions about what the community will discuss next week. Base each prediction
on themes that are rising or new this week, and give the reasoning and evidence behind it.

Be specific and factual. Do not invent discussions, releases, people, or numbers.

<%- if entries.any? -%>
## Sources

Base the document only on these numbered forum excerpts:

<%- entries.each do |entry| -%>
[<%= entry.number %>] "<%= entry.post_title %>" (posted <%= entry.posted_at.to_date.iso8601 %>, <%= entry.url %>)
<%= entry.content %>

<%- end -%>
<%- if trends.any? -%>
## Theme trends

How many excerpts each theme had per week, from <%= trend_weeks.first %> to <%= trend_weeks.last %> (this week last).
"rising" and "new" themes are growing: use them for your predictions.

<%- trends.each do |trend| -%>
- <%= trend.label %>: <%= trend.weekly_counts.values.join(", ") %> (<%= trend.classification %>)
<%- end -%>

<%- end -%>
Citation rule: end every sentence and every bullet with the numbers of the excerpts it is based on, in square
brackets, for example [2] or [1][4]. Each prediction must cite the excerpts that show its theme growing.
Only use numbers from 1 to <%= entries.size %>.
<%- else -%>
## Sources

No forum excerpts or theme trends are provided. Write from what you know about the Rails community.
<%- end -%>
